# Unblessed: sqlite values, rows and charges (#467); first blessing awaits human review.
# A Stub stands for the implementation's SQL values, which the Core converts:
# NULL to Nothing, INTEGER and REAL to numbers, a REAL by its shortest
# round-trip digits, TEXT to text and a BLOB to Bytes, each row a map in
# column order. A query never enrolls. An omitted or Nothing max is the
# binding's row cap, and each call charges max times perRow, 2, after its cost.
